            Mortgage Terms: 15 Years vs 30 Years
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Choosing between a 15-year and a 30-year home loan shapes your household budget for decades. Consider a $400,000 mortgage:
          </p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
              <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 font-bold uppercase text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3">Mortgage Option</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Interest Rate</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Monthly Payment</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Total Interest Paid</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Lifetime Total Cost</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">30-Year Fixed Term</td>
                  <td class="p-3">6.80%</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">$2,607.72</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-red-600 dark:text-red-400">$538,779.20</td>
                  <td class="p-3">$938,779.20</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">15-Year Fixed Term</td>
                  <td class="p-3">6.10%</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">$3,396.40</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">$211,352.00</td>
