          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            While the 15-year loan requires $788.68 more each month, it cuts lifetime interest costs by $327,427.20. Borrowers often select shorter mortgage durations when they hold ample emergency reserves and seek lower interest rates. Conversely, a 30-year term offers lower mandatory payments, allowing homeowners to align final debt retirement with Social Security or pension benefits while preserving cash flow during earlier career stages.
