              How does a loan payment calculator determine payoff time with extra monthly payments?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Under the Fixed Monthly Payment tab, you set your target monthly payment. Any amount above monthly accrued interest accelerates principal reduction. The calculator computes the exact number of months needed to bring the balance to zero and displays your debt free date.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
              Why do 72-month and 84-month car loans increase total car payment costs?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Extended car loan terms reduce monthly payments by stretching repayment over 6 to 7 years. Because interest compounds over a much longer duration, total borrowing costs escalate substantially. Additionally, rapid vehicle depreciation during early ownership can lead to negative equity.
            </p>
